1
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:39,620
What's drawing people from around the world to the southern Chinese city?

2
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:47,439
As Shenzhen prepares to host APEC 2026, I will explain later what APEC 2026 means.

3
00:00:47,439 --> 00:00:52,879
But people are flocking to this fishing village turned tech powerhouse of China.

4
00:00:52,879 --> 00:00:59,519
Home to such big names as Huawei, Tencent, DJI, the drone maker, and BYD and many other

5
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:06,040
tech giants, the city has grown from China's first special economic zone to a global hub

6
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:09,480
for innovation and advanced manufacturing.

7
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:12,359
And the momentum seems to be spiking.

8
00:01:12,359 --> 00:01:19,379
In the first seven months of this year, Shenzhen has recorded some 850,000 trips by visitors

9
00:01:19,379 --> 00:01:27,600
from Asia Pacific regions alone, up over 30% year on year, a record high for sure.

10
00:01:27,599 --> 00:01:29,759
What's special about this city?

11
00:01:29,759 --> 00:01:34,519
Has it become a regional or even global hub for innovation and the exchange of ideas?

12
00:01:34,519 --> 00:01:36,799
And why does it matter to you?

13
00:01:36,799 --> 00:01:42,879
Welcome to this special edition of The Point with me, Lu Xin, and Opinion Show, coming to you live from Beijing.

14
00:01:42,879 --> 00:01:48,039
I'm pleased to be joined from Auckland, New Zealand by Auntie Fit Le, a CSU professor

15
00:01:48,039 --> 00:01:53,000
at the University of Auckland and director of the New Zealand Asia Institute.

16
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:58,920
I'm Shenzhen by Fabienne Pacquore, executive vice president of CCI France-Chine, or the

17
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:04,000
French Chamber of Commerce in industry in China, and here in the studio by Jo Me, deputy

18
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:09,580
director of the Institute of American and Oceania Studies at the Chinese Academy of

19
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:12,680
International Trade and Economic Cooperation.

20
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:15,439
The warmest welcome to all of you.

21
00:02:15,439 --> 00:02:19,479
Now, let me go to Professor Fit Le first.

22
00:02:19,479 --> 00:02:25,359
I understand you are about to set foot in the city of Shenzhen with your students for

23
00:02:25,359 --> 00:02:29,639
